-- ==========================================================
-- 06 - PREDICTIVE ALERTS & SCHEDULED SERVICES
-- ==========================================================
-- PredictiveAlert history plus both alert-linked and standalone ScheduledService rows. Historical escalations are inserted Resolved-with-manual-schedule to avoid sp_AutoScheduleFromAlert's CURDATE()-based ScheduledDate; only a few live-today alerts go through the real trigger, and are inserted LAST so their auto-generated ScheduledService rows can't collide with our explicit ScheduleID values.
-- ==========================================================

-- PredictiveAlert -- 699 non-escalated rows (inserted first; none of these fire sp_AutoScheduleFromAlert)



-- ScheduledService -- 313 rows, all with explicit ScheduleID (244 left open for stage 07 to close via a real MaintenanceJob). Inserted here, before any escalated PredictiveAlert, so AUTO_INCREMENT hasn't handed out any IDs yet and our explicit values can't collide with sp_AutoScheduleFromAlert's.



-- PredictiveAlert -- 53 live escalations, inserted LAST. Each fires sp_AutoScheduleFromAlert for real; AUTO_INCREMENT now continues from 314 onward (past our highest explicit ScheduleID), so no collision.


